 "about_text": "Founded in 1989, Armory Center for the Arts is a nonprofit visual arts organization based in a historic 1932 California National Guard Armory building in Old Pasadena. It operates as a hybrid museum and art school, presenting contemporary art exhibitions alongside artist-led education programs for children, teens, and adults. Its roots trace back to the Pasadena Art Institute's Junior Museum program (1922), later evolving through the Pasadena Art Museum's Children's Art Workshop and the Pasadena Art Workshops before becoming the Armory in 1989. The organization emphasizes socially engaged, often BIPOC-centered contemporary art and free community-based art education, serving over 18,000 people annually across Pasadena and Los Angeles County, with particular focus on under-resourced neighborhoods and system-impacted communities.",
 "source_kind": "official",
